    "type": "WSI",
    "diagnosis": "<p>Nodular fasciitis</p>",
    "title": "",
    "legend": "<p>Right chest wall nodule presenting as a breast lump shows a spindle cell lesion with variable cellularity within adipose tissue. The spindle cells show bland vesicular nuclei, and are arranged in a focal storiform pattern. Oedematous stroma, scattered inflammatory cells and a few extravasated red blood cells are present. A few osteoclastic giant cells and occasional mitoses are seen. Immunohistochemistry shows positive reactivity of the spindle cells for SMA, with negative staining for epithelial markers, S100 and desmin.</p>",
    "source": "<p>SGH Pathology</p>",
